   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"FONT-SIZE:12pt;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Calibri&#39;;COLOR:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"FONT-SIZE:small;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Calibri&#39;;FONT-WEIGHT:normal;COLOR:rgb(0,0,0);FONT-STYLE:normal;TEXT-DECORATION:none;DISPLAY:inline\">The \r\nrattle book appears to be missing some chapters. I’m looking for information on \r\nhow to do survival analysis with Rattle. The survival guide for data mining that \r\nis out on the togaware site is for data mining with R not with Rattle. I’m \r\nlooking for better directions on how to use the interface not the scripting \r\nlanguage.</div></div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"FONT-SIZE:small;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Calibri&#39;;FONT-WEIGHT:normal;COLOR:rgb(0,0,0);FONT-STYLE:normal;TEXT-DECORATION:none;DISPLAY:inline\">B.<br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "z4em_rf2nesJ",
   "from": "Graham Williams",
   "author": "51ea28fc190ac537",
   "date": "2013-09-18T19:41:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: survival analysis with Rattle",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Survival Analysis is not covered in the Rattle book and is only minimally supported in Rattle.<br><br></div>On the Data tab, after loading a dataset, choose the Target Data Type as Survival. You can then choose the Time variable (time to event) and the Status variable (binary). Click Execute. Then on the Model tab Execute to build a Cox PH model. Some survival plots are then available. The Log tab shows the R commands if you need to do more, and ?coxph will provide further details.<br>\r\n\r\n</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Graham Williams<br><div><a href=\"http://togaware.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://togaware.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478805319000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1jUTYRqgBzdqExLqYu9-X9\">http://togaware.com</a></div></div></div>\r\n<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On 17 September 2013 06:18, Adaryl Wakefield <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">adaryl.l....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
